(1. LOOM TECHNOLOGY: THE TRADITIONAL LOIN LOOM \(PORKAPONG\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tangkhul weaving is executed exclusively by women on the indigenous) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(backstrap or loin loom \(Porkapong / Khashan-thing\). The loom consists of) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(lightweight bamboo and polished timber rods \(Tingkhor, Saphur, and) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Machor\) tensioned by the weaver's own body weight. This portable loom) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(permits exceptionally dense warp-faced weaves capable of withstanding) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(decades of highland wear.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
